  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Npc102503 and the CD276 antigen, as multiple pathways indicate that Npc102503 interacts with HaCaT cells, which are targeted by various compounds. These compounds, including 5,7,3',4',5'-Pentahydroxy-3,6,8-trimethoxyflavone, (1R,4R)-4-Hydroxydauca-7-Ene-6,9-Dione, and Hexyl Butanoate, all have a target of the CD276 antigen. The scores for these relationships range from 0.4735 to 0.5002, indicating a moderate level of confidence in the association. The presence of multiple compounds targeting the same antigen suggests a possible mechanism involving the CD276 antigen as a common target in these pathways. The integration of these findings implies that Npc102503 may influence the expression or activity of CD276 antigen through the activation of these compounds, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
